    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made the create endpoint reject with 409 only on a whole-key match.\n\n**`identityKey` definition** \u2014 `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`. Since the stored telephone is already E.164-normalized and the email is already lower-cased by the time an owner is persisted (and before the new owner is checked), the key is a straight concatenation of those normalized stored values.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived, `@Transient` `getIdentityKey()` computing the key from the stored `telephone`/`email`/`householdId`. Because MapStruct maps by getter name, this is automatically surfaced on the response DTO.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 `addOwner`:**\n   - Normalized telephone is now set on the owner *early* (before the check) instead of just before save.\n   - **Removed** the three separate 409 checks: the telephone-scan loop, the `isEmailAlreadyUsed` email check, and the `!sharesHousehold && !householdMembers.isEmpty()` household check (this deletes the old behaviour where same-household different-phone owners were rejected).\n   - **Added** one consolidated check: compute the new owner's `identityKey` (after the household-sharing block assigns its `householdId`, so an exact re-add into a shared household is still caught) and reject with 409 only if it exactly equals an existing owner's `identityKey`.\n   - The household-id propagation to existing members now runs *after* the check, so a rejected create has no side effects.\n   - Deleted the now-dead `isEmailAlreadyUsed` helper.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `identityKey` string property to the `Owner` response schema (the DTO is generated from this at build time), so the value is returned.\n\n### Behaviour result\n- Two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with **different** telephones now get different `identityKey`s and are **both allowed**.\n- Only an exact full-key match (same telephone **and** same email-or-empty **and** same householdId) is a duplicate \u2192 409.\n\nTest suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (same telephone \u21d2 same whole key \u21d2 409) passes, **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
